Flutter AirPlay Android native host for the shared Flutter application, GPL-3.0-only.

The Android playback implementation includes source derived from
jqssun/android-airplay-server, GPL-3.0-only, commit
c8defdd70d7e6a04f4f1b71d353653682d594106.
https://github.com/jqssun/android-airplay-server
Copyright holders are retained in upstream LICENSE and source notices.
Copied paths and pinned sources appear in dependencies.lock.json.
Changes: JNI host replaced to fit pinned UxPlay 1.73.7, Flutter embedded texture
and explicit NSD lifecycle; VideoRenderer error/output callbacks added.
Copied renderer classes use the tech.soit.flutterairplay.renderer namespace;
source notices and pinned upstream paths preserve provenance.

UxPlay is maintained directly in vendor/UxPlay; its upstream base is recorded
in vendor/UxPlay/UPSTREAM.md. GPL-3.0-or-later UxPlay,
LGPL-2.1-or-later libplist, Apache-2.0 OpenSSL, PlayFair and llhttp notices are
packaged under assets/licenses. See android/CORE_NOTICE.md.

Oboe 1.9.3, Copyright Google, Apache-2.0.
https://github.com/google/oboe
Apple ALAC decoder, Copyright (c) 2011 Apple Inc., Apache-2.0.
https://github.com/macosforge/alac
Pinned decoder-only sources and local input-bound checks reside in vendor/alac/.
AAC and AAC-ELD use Android MediaCodec. macOS audio uses AudioConverter.

Flutter SDK/engine are under the BSD-3-Clause license; standard Flutter
third-party engine notices are included by the Flutter build tool.
No DRM-protected video playback or HLS player is advertised by this host.

Shared C++ player: derived AirPlay audio configuration and Oboe device-loss
handling reside in native/player/. Kotlin MediaCodec/EGL playback and the
previous Android audio engine are replaced by the native platform adapters.
